## Code Implementation Guidelines

Follow these rules when you write code:

### General Patterns

- Use early returns whenever possible to make the code more readable.
- Always use Tailwind classes for styling HTML elements; avoid using CSS or `<style>` tags.
- Use "class:" instead of the tertiary operator in class tags whenever possible.
- Use descriptive variable and function/const names. Also, event functions should be named with a "handle" prefix, like "handleClick" for onClick and "handleKeyDown" for onKeyDown.
- Implement accessibility features on elements. For example, a tag should have a tabindex="0", aria-label, on:click, and on:keydown, and similar attributes.
- Use consts instead of functions, for example, "const toggle = () =>". Also, define a type if possible.

### Design System & Colors

- Use CSS variables for text hierarchy: `text-heading`, `text-body`, `text-muted` classes (not direct color values)
- Maintain WCAG AAA contrast ratios (7.2:1 for body text, 14.8:1 for headings)
- Use warm brown/beige palette throughout - avoid cool grays or blue tints
- For card backgrounds, use `bg-card` and `bg-card-hover` utility classes

### Component Standards

- Button component has 8 variants: default, primary, secondary, subtle, outline, ghost, link, destructive
- All interactive elements must have `cursor-pointer` class
- Use focus-visible ring styles: `focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary focus-visible:ring-offset-2`
- For subtle buttons or secondary actions, use `variant="subtle"` (light brown bg-primary/5)

### Animations

- For complex entrance animations, use CSS transitions with inline styles (not Tailwind's animate-in utilities)
- Pattern: useState for visibility + setTimeout trigger + transition-all duration-700 ease-out
- Mobile vs desktop animations should be responsive (check window.innerWidth in style prop)

### Cookie Consent & Analytics

- Analytics (GA/GTM) only load after user consent via AnalyticsProvider
- CookieConsent uses progressive disclosure (hide reject option initially)
- localStorage key: 'lgpd-cookie-consent' with values 'accepted' | 'rejected'
- X button dismisses without saving (nudge pattern to increase acceptance)
- Mobile: bottom sheet layout, Desktop: bottom-right card

### Accessibility

- All links and buttons need brown focus rings (not default blue)
- Use `rounded-sm` with focus-visible rings for proper visual feedback
- Maintain keyboard navigation support (tab order, enter/space activation)
- Include aria-label and title attributes for icon-only buttons
